$DIR/main.p:10:3: cannot store c in package variable kept, which outlives r
    c points into r. r is a local variable of f (declared at main.p:7). When f
    returns, r's memory is reclaimed, but package variables live for the whole
    program, so package variable kept would be left pointing at reclaimed
    memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of r, or allocate r and store its owner, an
    owned[ring[Conn, 4]], which moves there:
        kept = new(ring[Conn, 4])
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
